x01-core-alignment patch 05-float-halo-state (git apply ignores this header)

E7 item: (b) Float storage of halo state. Precision only: the store conditions are already as
SAGE26 (evidence in the report), so there is no b-cond item.

SAGE26 behaviour: struct GALAXY holds Mvir, deltaMvir, Rvir, Vvir and Vmax (R/src/core_allvars.h:129-133)
and infallMvir, infallVvir and infallVmax (R/src/core_allvars.h:198-200) as float members. They are
stored at creation (init_galaxy, R/src/model_misc.c:113-118, :189-191), at the first-occupied
Type 0/1 update (R/src/core_build_model.c:262-271: Vmax; deltaMvir = new_Mvir - Mvir, the double
new mass less the float stored one; Rvir and Vvir only when new_Mvir > Mvir; then Mvir = new_Mvir),
at a central's infall into a satellite (:307-309, from the double copies of the float members at
:247-249) and at the orphan transition (:324-325 deltaMvir = -Mvir, Mvir = 0; :331-333 infall
values). No other R/src code assigns these members.

Mimic behaviour replaced: the core declares the eight as double (src/core/core_properties.yaml:126-219;
Vmax is float in simulations/mini-millennium/halo_properties.yaml:112-120) and stores the double
values at the same points with the same conditions: init_new_halo (src/core/inheritance.c:97-107,
through the generated init_halo_from_payload), apply_descendant_properties
(src/core/inheritance.c:40-77) and make_orphan (src/core/inheritance.c:79-95).

What the patch changes: each of those stores is rounded through float, (double)(float)x, the fields
staying double: Mvir, deltaMvir, Rvir, Vvir and Vmax in apply_descendant_properties, deltaMvir and the
three infall values in make_orphan, the three infall values on the Type 0 -> 1 transition, and Mvir,
Rvir, Vvir and Vmax after init_halo_from_payload in init_new_halo. The conditions are unchanged; the
Rvir/Vvir test now compares the double new mass with the float-rounded stored mass, as SAGE26 does.
Vmax is float already, so its rounding is a no-op, kept for completeness. No declared type and no
output dataset type changes.

Reading for i02: yes, it would change sage16's output (every module reading the core halo values
reads the rounded ones, and Mvir, deltaMvir and the infall values are written as stored) and
halos-only's (it writes Mvir, deltaMvir and the infall values as stored, and a Type 2 row's stored
Rvir and Vvir), at the float-rounding level for the written values.

diff --git a/src/core/inheritance.c b/src/core/inheritance.c
index b3ab75cb..963c12d5 100644
--- a/src/core/inheritance.c
